From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: media: venus: vdec: submit capture buffers restarted during a seek

GStreamer's v4l2 decoders seek with STREAMOFF on both queues, then
STREAMON on CAPTURE first and OUTPUT second. vdec_start_capture() returns
early while the output queue is off, so the capture buffers queued before
STREAMON are never handed to the firmware, and vdec_start_output() in the
SEEK state only re-queues the DPB buffers (and only if streamon_cap is
set). A decoder without separate DPB buffers (Venus 1.x on MSM8916) then
has nothing to decode into: the firmware stops consuming input and the
seek never completes. On SM-T550 every GNOME Showtime start (it seeks
after preroll) froze on the first frame, and so did any later seek.

When OUTPUT is restarted in the SEEK state while CAPTURE is streaming but
was never started by the driver, submit the capture buffers waiting in
the m2m context after the first input buffers, as vdec_start_capture()
would have done, and mark capture as started.

Capture buffers queued while CAPTURE streams but OUTPUT is still off would
normally go to the firmware straight from buf_queue, and then be submitted
a second time by the above (Venus 1.8 firmware: Err_Fatal in vbuffer.c and
a system error). So hold them back in the m2m context during a seek, like
the pre-STREAMON ones, and submit them all in one place.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -1125,8 +1125,29 @@
 
 			if (inst->streamon_cap) {
 				ret = venus_helper_queue_dpb_bufs(inst);
+				if (ret)
+					return ret;
+			} else if (vb2_is_streaming(v4l2_m2m_get_dst_vq(inst->m2m_ctx))) {
+				/*
+				 * The capture queue was restarted while the output
+				 * queue was off (a seek: STREAMOFF both, STREAMON
+				 * capture, STREAMON output), so vdec_start_capture()
+				 * returned early and the capture buffers are waiting
+				 * in the m2m context (vdec_vb2_buf_queue() holds them
+				 * back during a seek). Hand them to the firmware now,
+				 * after the first input buffers: a decoder without
+				 * DPB buffers decodes straight into them and
+				 * otherwise stalls for good.
+				 */
+				ret = venus_helper_queue_dpb_bufs(inst);
+				if (ret)
+					return ret;
+
+				ret = venus_helper_process_initial_cap_bufs(inst);
 				if (ret)
 					return ret;
+
+				inst->streamon_cap = 1;
 			}
 		}
 		goto done;
@@ -1390,6 +1411,19 @@
 		v4l2_m2m_buf_done(vbuf, VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE);
 		v4l2_event_queue_fh(&inst->fh, &eos);
 		inst->next_buf_last = false;
+		mutex_unlock(&inst->lock);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * During a seek, keep capture buffers in the m2m context until the
+	 * output queue is restarted: vdec_start_output() hands all of them to
+	 * the firmware after the first input buffers. Submitting them here as
+	 * well would give the firmware the same buffer twice.
+	 */
+	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_CAPTURE(vb->vb2_queue->type) &&
+	    inst->codec_state == VENUS_DEC_STATE_SEEK && !inst->streamon_out) {
+		v4l2_m2m_buf_queue(inst->m2m_ctx, vbuf);
 		mutex_unlock(&inst->lock);
 		return;
 	}
